Thursday Update
 * Trade Alert: Sold Cigna calls for big gain; Oracle calls higher*&nbsp;St=
ocks swoon as investors fear rise of credit rates&nbsp;Stocks fell Thursday=
 fell as government bond yields continued to rise and economists cast doubt=
 over the surprise drop in initial weekly jobless claims.The Dow Jones Indu=
strial Average fell by 1%, to 31,657.07. S&amp;P 500 was down by 1.4% to 3,=
870.73 and Nasdaq was lower by 2.2% to 13,299.93. Technology and consumer d=
iscretionary led the worst performers, with all sectors in the red after mi=
dday on Thursday.The US 10-year yield surged by 6.9 basis points to 1.46%, =
its highest level in about a year.The surprisingly large 111,000 drop in in=
itial jobless claims reflects special factors, particularly in Texas, that =
could result in a rebound next week, Jefferies economists said in a researc=
h note. Overall, the number of claims fell to 730,000 over a week through F=
eb 20, its lowest level in three months, according to the US Bureau of Labo=
r Statistics."So, either we are totally off in our interpretation of the im=
pact of these storms on the (Texas) labor market, or the storms/outages wer=
e so disruptive that people were unable to file," Simons and Markowska said=
. "Next week's data will be telling. We think (the) decline this week shoul=
d be viewed with caution."Meanwhile, the US economy expanded by 4.1% annual=
ized in the fourth quarter, versus an advance estimate of 4% growth, accord=
ing to data compiled by Trading Economics.In company news, Gamestop (GME) s=
hares jumped 45% intraday. The gain was supported by news of Chief Financia=
l Officer Jim Bell's resignation on Tuesday, with Reddit investors taking i=
t as a signal of a likely positive turnaround for the company.Twitter (TWTR=
) outlined "ambitious" plans Thursday to at least double revenue by 2023 af=
ter the number of users surge during the COVID-19 pandemic and last year's =
US elections. Shares jumped by 6.9%.Portfolio: Our Cigna calls sold at seco=
nd target for 65% gain, which is great. Our ORCL calls are up sharply; adju=
st targets and stop. BA calls order did not fill. No new recommendation.*CU=
